  "description": "A parametric PLANTER BOX on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nFOUR WALLS AND A BASE AROUND A SOIL BLOCK, not a box with a lid, so the soil is its own piece at its own level and the published soil volume is the number a landscaper orders against. The rim and the soil level come out separately because the gap between them is what stops the soil washing over the edge.\n\nTHE PLANTING IS A CIRCLE ROW spread along the box at even pitch — the plan symbol for shrubs, one row for any number of them, from zero to eight. Zero plants is a legitimate answer: an empty trough is still a planter.\n\nTHREE SHAPES. Rectangular and Trough share the four-wall construction; Round abandons it for a ring, and takes the soil with it — a round pot with mitred corners would be nonsense.",
