            {
              "id": "modelling_plan",
              "name": "Modelling plan (for Blender / engine agents)",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "PLANTER BOX — MODELLING PLAN (surface draft; to be refined)\nMetres unless stated; values in braces are this object's parameters. Z up, floor at Z 0. Hosted on a point: origin at the placement point on the floor.\n\nWHAT IT IS\ncorten steel planter box, trailing greenery, gravel mulch\n\nGEOMETRY\nModel the object described above as clean, closed meshes with real thickness and small bevels on exposed edges (about 2 mm) so highlights catch. Drive every dimension from these parameters:\n- Length: {length}\n- Width: {width}\n- Height: {height}\n- Wall thickness: {wallThk}\n- Soil depth below rim: {soilDepth}\n- Plants: {plants}\n- Plant radius: {plantRadius}\n- Shape: {shape} (one of: Rectangular / Round / Trough)\n- Show planting: {showPlants}\n- Rotation (deg): {rotation}\n- Anchor Direction: {anchorDir} (one of: Top-Left / Top-Center / Top-Right / Left-Center / Center / Right-Center / Bottom-Left / Bottom-Center / Bottom-Right)\n- Margin from host: {margin}\n- Flip side: {flipSide}\nKeep the proportions of a well-made real product; add the secondary detail a close-up render needs (joints, reveals, fixings) but no hidden interior geometry.\n\nMATERIALS\n- Base colour: {baseColor}\n- Roughness: {roughness}\nPrincipled BSDF per visible part, using the colour and roughness above for the main surface; secondary parts in a neutral complementary finish. Use Object / box-projected texture coordinates (no UVs needed). Add a subtle noise bump (strength ~0.03) so surfaces are not perfectly flat.\n\nLIGHTS\nNone. This object does not emit light.\n\nCHECKS (measure after building)\n- Length = {length}\n- Width = {width}\n- Height = {height}\n- Soil depth below rim = {soilDepth}\n- Plant radius = {plantRadius}\n- All meshes closed, no duplicate faces, origin as stated above.",
